{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1454402-lmg-and-hmg-stats","id":1454402,"title":"LMG and HMG stats?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-06T18:10:18-07:00","id":1454402,"title":"LMG and HMG stats?","content":"The Hurt Locker mentions Machines Guns (M-60's, 50 Cal, etc) but doesn't include the stats for them on the charts, they should have been just before the Grenade Launchers. Of course these are not everyday weapons but sometimes our mortal characters want to hose down a zombie horde with a crew served weapon in the cause of survival. 1st Edition NWoD had stats in the Arms and Armoury book but we don't have stats for CoD versions with the init penalties and etc, that I have seen. Can someone point me at the stats?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26704-fortunae","name":"Fortunae","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T18:25:20-07:00","id":1454404,"title":"","content":"Damage for a &quot;Light Machine Gun&quot; (firing an intermediate rifle round - 5.56x45mm NATO for example) would be 3 damage. Your medium/general purpose machine guns firing a full power rifle round (e.g., 7.62x51mm NATO) would do 4 damage. A .50 BMG heavy machine gun round would be 5 damage. High Capacity for all of them.<br /> <br /> The other stat stuff for concealment, initiative, etc., I'm not as sure about. I would probably give a -5 initiative, size 4 for the LMG and MMG. The .50 HMGs aren't generally man portable for CofD combat purposes. Maybe size 6, initiative -5 for a superhuman carrying one?<br /> <br /> So say an M249 would be:<br /> Damage 3, Capacity High, Initiative -5, Size 4, Availability 5.<br /> <br /> And an M60 would be:<br /> Damage 4, Capacity High, Initiative -5, Size 4, Availability 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 09-28-2021, 10:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T19:53:00-07:00","id":1454409,"title":"","content":"If you\u2019re using the capacity rules then belt-fed machine guns need to be \u201cextreme capacity\u201d and only run out of ammo on a dramatic failure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T18:00:34-07:00","id":1461894,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I really appreciate your help with this!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26704-fortunae","name":"Fortunae","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T19:49:23-07:00","id":1461906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1454402-lmg-and-hmg-stats?p=1454409#post1454409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you\u2019re using the capacity rules then belt-fed machine guns need to be \u201cextreme capacity\u201d and only run out of ammo on a dramatic failure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good catch, I didn't even notice there was an Extreme capacity in Hurt Locker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}